│    execution.                                                      │
│  • It then calls self.create_agent_executor and executes the task  │
│    prompt, handles retries and errors.                             │
│  • Finally, it returns the resulting output string.                │
│                                                                    │
│  2 Relationship to the bug:                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • The issue is about creating a Task with context explicitly set  │
│    as an empty list (e.g., context=[]), but still receiving        │
│    context strings from previous tasks.                            │
│  • In the execute_task method, the presence of context is checked  │
│    via "if context:" (line 251). In Python, an empty list          │
│    context=[] is a falsy value. Therefore, the check should        │
│    prevent the context string from being appended when context=[]. │
│  • However, the "context" parameter's typehint is Optional[str],   │
│    so context is expected to be a string or None. If context is    │
│    passed as a list (e.g., []), this could be causing unexpected   │
│    behavior or the context value from elsewhere is still being     │
│    appended.                                                       │
│  • Another possibility is that memory or knowledge context is      │
│    being appended unconditionally or incorrectly when context=[].  │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Intended behavior:                                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • When context=[] or an empty context equivalent is passed, the   │
│    final task prompt should not include any context string from    │
│    previous tasks.                                                 │
│  • The check "if context:" should prevent any context addition in  │
│    that case.                                                      │
│  • The memory and knowledge contextual info should also respect an │
│    empty or no context scenario and not append unrelated context.  │
│                                                                    │
